Description: ASoC: fsl: imx-ssi: don't register the FIQ PCM on a DMA board
 Both the FIQ and the dmaengine PCM register on the SSI's device, so
 both bind to a card that names it as platform, and each keeps its own
 state in the runtime's private_data. Whichever opens last wins: on the
 Chumby Classic (IMX_SSI_DMA) the FIQ PCM's open replaced the dmaengine
 PCM's, and hw_params dereferenced a NULL DMA channel. A board that
 asks for DMA now gets only the DMA PCM.
Author: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AI generated code]
Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Ee1gRFAS7tp8oLbvQ
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/fsl/imx-ssi.c b/sound/soc/fsl/imx-ssi.c
index f8488e8f5..1e26d2603 100644
--- a/sound/soc/fsl/imx-ssi.c
+++ b/sound/soc/fsl/imx-ssi.c
@@ -595,7 +595,14 @@ static int imx_ssi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	ssi->fiq_params.dma_params_rx = &ssi->dma_params_rx;
 	ssi->fiq_params.dma_params_tx = &ssi->dma_params_tx;
 
-	ssi->fiq_init = imx_pcm_fiq_init(pdev, &ssi->fiq_params);
+	/*
+	 * Both PCMs would bind to this device and share the runtime's
+	 * private data, so a board that asks for DMA gets only DMA.
+	 */
+	if (ssi->flags & IMX_SSI_DMA)
+		ssi->fiq_init = -ENODEV;
+	else
+		ssi->fiq_init = imx_pcm_fiq_init(pdev, &ssi->fiq_params);
 	ssi->dma_init = imx_pcm_dma_init(pdev, IMX_SSI_DMABUF_SIZE);
 
 	if (ssi->fiq_init && ssi->dma_init) {
